# Secret-Safe Integration Workflow

## Rule

Credential values never belong in source control, Redis, THINK, DTHINK,
screenshots, logs, agent prompts, or PR comments. Agents may report only a
secret name and whether it is configured.

## Sources

- Production secrets: hosting-provider secret manager.
- Local development: ignored `.env` loaded by standalone scripts.
- Upstash Redis MCP: operational Redis commands only; never use it as a secret
  vault or search it for credential values.
- Upstash Box: `UPSTASH_BOX_API_KEY` from the environment only.
- GitHub and Heroku: their APIs may be used through scoped runtime tokens, but
  token values are never printed or persisted.

## Reusable gates

- `npm run verify:secrets` checks tracked files and reports configured names
  without printing values.
- `npm run verify:box-web` runs an HTTP staging check inside Upstash Box when
  `UPSTASH_BOX_API_KEY` is configured; otherwise it reports an explicit skip.
- `npm run verify:box-web -- --strict` is used only in an environment that has
  provisioned the Box key and should fail when the key is absent.

## Upstash Box + Redis test env (see box-redis-test-environment.snippet)

- Persistent Box: `coherent-beagle-67807` — PAUSE after use, NEVER delete.
- Fetch box key via Heroku API (name-only reporting), never print the value.
- Redis MCP: operational commands only; never a secret vault.

## Agent behavior

Agents must not ask for a credential value when the environment can report its
presence. They must use the named secret source, redact process output, and
record only the variable name, source, and verification status.
